Phase 1 prep for P10. No production source is touched: this commit adds one
test file and nothing else. It is EXPECTED TO FAIL until P10 lands; the failure
list is P10's work queue.

The gate has two clauses — "no timer fires more often than once a second" AND
"every repeating timer is cleared on visibilitychange" — and a site passes only
when both hold. That is how 0-D2-03 measured the code, and it is what this test
implements. Against origin/staging it reports 20 violations across 21
setInterval sites, file and line, matching the landed inventory site for site.
The one pass is useEngagementHeartbeat.ts, the pattern P10 copies.

A source scan, not a runtime test: the 21 sites live in pages, hooks and ad
shells, several behind an admin role or an active judging session, and the ones
nobody mounted would be exactly the ones that regress.

Deliberately generous to existing code and never harsher than the gate: the
visibilitychange clause is satisfied when a file mentions the event and calls
clearInterval, without proving they are wired together. Nothing that satisfies
the gate can fail this check, so every violation it reports is real. Tighten
when P10 lands; do not loosen. An interval that cannot be resolved statically
counts as a violation — unknown is not a pass (C-34).

Five control tests run the same scanner over synthetic sources and prove it
rejects a 200 ms timer that does handle visibilitychange, a 30 s timer that does
not, an unresolvable delay, and resolves 1800/60 to 30 ms — so the checker is
proved able to fail independently of src/, and stays proved after the list
above is empty.

Two refinements to the inventory, recorded not tidied: useJudgeSession.ts:173
resolves to HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL = 30_000 (§3 shows "?"), and Index.tsx:191
resolves to 30 ms, which confirms §3's note and corrects its Interval cell ("1").
Both remain violations either way.

npx tsc -b tsconfig.json exit 0; eslint clean; full suite 2486 passed with the
two expected failures (this file's gate assertion, and the pre-existing stale
typecheckIsNotVacuous assertion routed as F-60).

